Revision history for App-Actions - run GitHub Actions workflows locally

0.002.0
	- The test that walks t/fixtures now checks each example against its
	  schema as it reads it, so a fixture with the wrong shape is named
	  and rejected there, like one that is not valid JSON, and does not
	  count towards the schema coverage check.
	- make check-staged and make check-worktree now list each check they
	  ran, as passed (with its test count) or failed, and each they skipped,
	  so a clean run shows that the live-knob check ran rather than only
	  that nothing failed.  A commit that passes the hook is still silent.
	- t/regex.t's time limits are scaled up when Devel::Cover is loaded.
	  The CI coverage job runs the suite under it, which made the
	  40,000-comparison tokenizer case (linear, but about five times
	  slower there) fail its two-second limit.
	- Documented the configuration that Object::Configure adds to
	  App::Actions->new and action-run: an App__Actions section in the
	  Config::Abstraction files (base/local in CONFIG_DIR or ~/.conf) and
	  App__Actions__* environment variables, both of which win over the
	  arguments and the command line and are not validated.

0.001.0	Thu Oct 22 12:40:02 PM EDT 2026
	- First release
